veys show the contest essentially tied, with Drazan holding a nominal edge in the most recent polls within the margin of error. Expert raters are split between Lean D and Likely D, and prediction markets give Kotek roughly a three-in-four chance of winning a second term.\n\nThe race has centered on public safety and affordability, themes that dominated the first debate in early October. Kotek's incumbency and Oregon's partisan baseline give her the structural advantage, but the polling picture leaves little room for error, making this one of the closer gubernatorial contests of the cycle.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.91, "margin": 7.23}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7143, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6673, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6685, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7753, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7762, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7967, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7478, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.743, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7131, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7358, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7337, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7182, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7487, "margin": 3.5}]}